# Explicit Question-to-Answer Procedure

Status: DONE
Milestone: A0 Procedure definition only
Dependencies: None
Execution status: IN_PROGRESS (local draft/snapshot only; no Azure execution)

## Purpose

Define the intended dictate/select/Ask/stream flow without automatically uploading a meeting.

## Inputs

Implemented source-scoped draft/commit/answer components; approved Azure profile and silent auth;
current capture policy; explicit owner-selected question. None of those future answer components
is implied implemented by this authored procedure.

## Procedure

1. Keep ordinary Computer/Mic transcription local and source-separated.
2. Owner selects known transcript segments, arms a Mic question span, or types the question.
3. Show the editable draft and whether it includes provisional text. No chat/clipboard-history reading.
4. For Ask-as-shown, freeze exactly that displayed revision. For Finish dictation, enqueue/ack the
   source commit first; never use global Stop or silently send a fallback revision.
5. On explicit Ask, create one request bound to the immutable snapshot/profile/context policy.
6. Acquire a cached/silent token; if interaction is required, retain the draft and show SignInRequired.
7. Stream one foreground stateless model request. No tools, server conversation or unselected meeting context.
8. Render bounded text batches in the existing HWND, with question identity and honest terminal status.
9. Cancel/replacement/hide/lock/failure invalidate that request's future UI events; preserve partial output as incomplete.
10. Record only timings/counts/result metadata. Save/export Q/A only on explicit action.

## Stop conditions

Missing approved profile/auth/network route, empty/oversized draft, ambiguous source/session/revision,
commit failure, revoked capture readiness, rejected/filtered/incomplete stream, unsupported model
parameters or exhausted retry/deadline budget. Do not change provider/region/data policy automatically.

## Tasks

- [x] Define manual egress, source/snapshot boundaries and streamed lifecycle.
- [x] Preserve no-repeat permission/rehearsal confirmations and local-ASR/Docker-last direction.
- [x] Separate authored procedure from future execution evidence.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Procedure cannot imply automatic meeting upload, background answer generation or cloud-ASR fallback.
- [x] Failure retains inspectable local state instead of a success-shaped or silently changed answer.

